
XSD - XML Schema Definition :
---------------------------

XSD, or XML Schema Definition, is a W3C recommendation that defines the structure and content of an
XML document. It's a formal way to describe the legal building blocks of an XML document, including
elements, attributes, data types, default values, and the order and number of elements. XSD is used
to validate XML documents and ensure they adhere to the defined rules, guaranteeing consistency
and reliability